{"assets":["/statement-assets/89303f8f2f7ecd5e98568fe2a8c03b5b7d44f5c35e50b883a4b23417ad561533.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2077","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Another Folding Strip"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For an array $$$b$$$ of length $$$m$$$, define $$$f(b)$$$ as follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a $$$1 \\times m$$$ strip, where all cells initially have darkness $$$0$$$. You want to transform it into a strip where the color at the $$$i$$$-th position has darkness $$$b_i$$$. You can perform the following operation, which consists of two steps:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Fold the paper at any line between two cells. You may fold as many times as you like, or choose not to fold at all."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" position to drop the black dye. The dye permeates from the top and flows down to the bottom, increasing the darkness of all cells in its path by $$$1$$$. After dropping the dye, you unfold the strip."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$f(b)$$$ be the minimum number of operations required to achieve the desired configuration. It can be proven that the goal can always be achieved in a finite number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of length $$$n$$$. Evaluate"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$\\sum_{l=1}^n\\sum_{r=l}^n f(a_l a_{l+1} \\ldots a_r)$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — denoting the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of all values of $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the required sum modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n0 1 0\n6\n1 0 0 1 2 1\n5\n2 1 2 4 3\n12\n76 55 12 32 11 45 9 63 88 83 32 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n28\n47\n7001\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_1)=f(\\mathtt{0})=0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_1a_2)=f(\\mathtt{01})=1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_1a_2a_3)=f(\\mathtt{010})=1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_2)=f(\\mathtt{1})=1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_2a_3)=f(\\mathtt{10})=1$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$f(a_3)=f(\\mathtt{0})=0$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This sums up to $$$0+1+1+1+1+0 = 4$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$f(a_1a_2a_3a_4a_5a_6) = 2$$$. Here's one possible sequence of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/89303f8f2f7ecd5e98568fe2a8c03b5b7d44f5c35e50b883a4b23417ad561533.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2077E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2077/problem/E"}